// ── Booking & money ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// P05 wires these to the Booking / Payment models. Declared here so the
// whole enum surface lands in one migration rather than dribbling across
// two.

enum BookingStatus {
  PENDING
  CONFIRMED
  CANCELLED
  COMPLETED
  NO_SHOW
}

/// How a booking was made (#380). `ONLINE` is a player in the app or on the
/// web; `DESK` is the club booking on someone's behalf (#364), which is where a
/// recurring series comes from too. Only ONLINE counts toward the club's cap on
/// a player's upcoming online bookings.
enum BookingChannel {
  ONLINE
  DESK
}

enum PaymentStatus {
  REQUIRES_ACTION
  PAID
  FAILED
  REFUNDED
  PARTIALLY_REFUNDED
}

enum Locale {
  bg
  en
}

/// Who or what performed an audited action.
///
/// SYSTEM is not "no actor" — it is a deliberate claim that no human chose
/// this. A directory-driven role sync is SYSTEM even though it changes a
/// person's access, and telling that apart from an administrator doing it by
/// hand is most of the value of an audit trail.
enum AuditActorType {
  USER
  SYSTEM
  API_KEY
}

/// NOTE: a PLATFORM value was drafted here for a club-side mirror of platform
/// access, then removed before it shipped. The owner decided platform reads are
/// recorded in `platform_audit_entry` only and are NOT surfaced in a club's own
/// audit log. Nothing would have written PLATFORM, and Postgres cannot DROP an
/// enum value — so adding it speculatively is a one-way door. If that decision
/// is revisited, adding it then is a one-line migration.

/// External identity providers a club can federate with.
enum IdentityProviderType {
  ENTRA_ID
}

/// Which APNs host a device token belongs to.
///
/// These are different servers with different token namespaces
/// (api.sandbox.push.apple.com vs api.push.apple.com). A token minted for one
/// is rejected by the other with BadDeviceToken, which reads as a broken
/// certificate and is not.
enum ApnsEnvironment {
  SANDBOX
  PRODUCTION
}

/// What a `VenuePhoto` is (#366). One COVER per venue (a partial unique index
/// in P47); any number of GALLERY photos, capped by the use case.
enum VenuePhotoKind {
  COVER
  GALLERY
}
